      "writtenOn": "2020-01-28T14:36:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we could eliminate this if statement by making startPollingForConnector() call mConnectorSupplier.get() before calling Thread.sleep().\n\nThe benefit would be fewer codepaths and more reliable code, and initialization code is often hard to test. On the minus side, the common case of creating a TetheringManager for the first time while the system is already running would perform worse because it would need to create a thread (after the first time, SystemServiceRegistry caches the manager object so it doesn\u0027t matter). The overhead of creating the thread should be a small fraction of a millisecond, which seems negligible; we might be able to optimize it further by using ConnectivityThread; see below.\n\nOne drawback of doing this would be that if the app calls TetheringManager methods immediately after the manager class is constructed, then those methods would run on the polling thread, whereas subsequent methods would run on the app thread. In certain unlikely cases this is an app-visible difference. Given the other comments in this file related to the effects of running manager code in different threads, what you have here seems safer. It can still have this problem, but only if the app constructs a tetheringmanager immediately after boot.\n\nWe should probably try to capture this in a comment somewhere.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 176,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 180,
        "endChar": 9
      },
