      "writtenOn": "2020-01-28T14:36:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are the app-visible implications of this if? ISTM that if the connector is already available, then app calls will proceed on their own thread, and potentially (very unlikely) get RemoteExceptions on those threads, and if not, exceptions will be seen by the polling thread. But that\u0027s already covered by my comment on line 222.\n\nIn addition, are there any ordering issues? Given that all calls are executed in sequence (due to how onTetheringConnected works), and all binder IPCs are oneway to the same binder object on the other side, perhaps not.\n\nOne reason this is safe is that none of the app-called methods assume they\u0027re running on any particular thread. However, if those methods were somehow to execute app code (like a lambda passed in by the app), then that could contain non-threadsafe code that could fail if it\u0027s run sometimes on the polling thread and sometimes on the app thread.\n\nMight want to add a comment here about this.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 239,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 239,
        "endChar": 14
      },
